## Prerequisites

This plan's file changes are all inside `src/tools/init/` except for the
orchestrator prompt, which belongs to a separate scope. The orchestrator
prompt update is part of this intent shift but the file lives outside the
plan's scope directory, so it is declared here and executed as a sibling
plan before (or alongside) this one.

- `.claude/commands/aide/init.md` must be updated to the new branch logic
  before a user-facing release is cut. Contract this plan consumes from the
  prompt: the agent calls `aide_init` without `category` first, inspects
  each category's step statuses, silently calls `aide_init` with
  `category=X` for pure-create categories (only `would-create` /
  `would-skip` / `exists` statuses), uses `AskUserQuestion` for categories
  that contain any `would-overwrite` step or for inherent decisions
  (framework, brain path, MCP merge, IDE choice). If that file is not
  updated in lockstep, the host agent will still ask per-category on
  cold-start — the tool contract below stays correct but the UX regression
  the spec exists to remove will persist. Produce the companion plan for
  that file as its own `plan.aide` (single-module-scoping rule) before
  this plan's step 9 runs.

