### 2. Create the shared byte-compare helper

Read:
- `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions` — aggressive modularization, folder-name-is-function-name, JSDoc-on-every-function
- `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure` — shared-submodules-within-a-domain escalation path

- [x] 2a. Create `src/tools/init/shared/compareBytes/index.ts` with a default-exported async function `compareBytes(filePath: string, canonicalBytes: string): Promise<"would-create" | "would-skip" | "would-overwrite">`. Contract: stat/read `filePath`; return `"would-create"` when the file does not exist (ENOENT), `"would-skip"` when the file exists and its bytes are byte-identical to `canonicalBytes`, `"would-overwrite"` when the file exists and its bytes differ. Non-ENOENT read errors propagate. The return type uses only the three planning statuses that map from disk state; callers convert a matching file into `"exists"` or `"would-skip"` depending on their semantics (see step 3 and per-helper rationale in Decisions).
- [x] 2b. Create `src/tools/init/shared/compareBytes/index.test.ts` with Vitest unit tests: missing file returns `"would-create"`; matching bytes return `"would-skip"`; differing bytes return `"would-overwrite"`; non-ENOENT errors (simulate with a directory at the path) rethrow. Co-locate per playbook convention. Use a temp directory per test (`mkdtemp` / `rm -r`) following the pattern already used in `applySteps/index.test.ts`.

